  {
   "title": "Buying and Selling 🏪",
   "text": "In a shop, each thing has a PRICE — the money it costs. The buyer pays the money, and the seller gives the thing. A pencil for ₹5 means we pay ₹5 to buy it!",
   "emoji": "🏪",
   "bgColor": "from-amber-400 to-orange-500",
   "spoken": "Every thing in a shop has a price. We pay money to buy it.",
   "diagram": {
    "type": "generic-flow",
    "animate": true,
    "title": "How buying works",
    "data": {
     "steps": [
      "Price tag ₹5",
      "You pay ₹5",
      "Pencil is yours!"
     ]
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "title": "Add the Prices 🧮",
   "text": "Buying many things? ADD the prices! A pencil ₹5 and an eraser ₹3: 5 plus 3 makes 8. Pay ₹8 and take both!",
   "emoji": "🧮",
   "bgColor": "from-blue-400 to-indigo-500",
   "spoken": "Add the prices to find how much to pay.",
   "diagram": {
    "type": "generic-flow",
    "animate": true,
    "title": "Adding prices",
    "data": {
     "steps": [
      "Pencil ₹5",
      "+ Eraser ₹3",
      "= Pay ₹8"
     ]
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "title": "Pay the EXACT Money 🎯",
   "text": "Paying exactly means using the right notes and coins — no more, no less! Something costs ₹12? A ₹10 note and a ₹2 coin make exactly ₹12. Perfect payment!",
   "emoji": "🎯",
   "bgColor": "from-emerald-400 to-teal-500",
   "spoken": "Exact money means the notes and coins add up to the price.",
   "diagram": {
    "type": "generic-flow",
    "animate": true,
    "title": "Exact payment",
    "data": {
     "steps": [
      "Cost ₹12",
      "₹10 + ₹2",
      "= ₹12 exactly!"
     ]
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "title": "Change: Pay More, Get Some Back 🔁",
   "text": "If you pay MORE than the price, the shopkeeper gives money BACK. That is called CHANGE! Price ₹15, you pay ₹20: change = 20 − 15 = ₹5.",
   "emoji": "🔁",
   "bgColor": "from-purple-400 to-pink-500",
   "spoken": "Change is the money you get back when you pay more than the price.",
   "diagram": {
    "type": "generic-flow",
    "animate": true,
    "title": "Getting change",
    "data": {
     "steps": [
      "Price ₹15",
      "You pay ₹20",
      "Change ₹5"
     ]
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "title": "Count Your Money Before Shopping 👛",
   "text": "Good shoppers count their money FIRST! You have ₹20. A chocolate costs ₹12. After buying, 20 − 12 = ₹8 is left. Now you know what you can still buy!",
   "emoji": "👛",
   "bgColor": "from-rose-400 to-red-500",
   "spoken": "Subtract to see how much money is left after buying.",
   "diagram": {
